#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186173277 :tutorial/content "To evaluate a large exponent, we first write out the power using multiplication signs as usual. Then, we calculate the product by splitting it into groups of two-digit multiplications, before calculating the resulting product. \n\nFor example, let's evaluate $2^4.$\n\nFirst, we write\n![](images/4c/4ccd929bbf46272fe64264465ed639c841643ec0e6c42d053d66555faa910dff.svg)\n\nSince $2 \\times 2 = 4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} \\times \\underbrace{2 \\times 2}_{\\large \\color{blue}4} = {\\color{blue}4} \\times {\\color{blue}4}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $4\\times 4.$\nSince $4\\times 4=16,$ we conclude that \n\n$$\n2^4=16.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "4a00be57-d26e-53b8-9d16-7f4994f21077" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8955 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
